    "body": "GDPR requires us to add a Privacy Policy document to the site explaining how we handle all of the data in plain English. I assume that English would be enough and that we don't have to translate it in all the different languages.\r\n\r\nmore resources available at:\r\n\r\n- https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/privacy-notices-transparency-and-control/what-should-you-include-in-your-privacy-notice/\r\n- https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/privacy-notices-transparency-and-control/privacy-notices-under-the-eu-general-data-protection-regulation/\r\n\r\n### Todo\r\n\r\n- [x] gather information on what to include in the \"Privacy Policy\"\r\n- [x] write \"Privacy Policy\" in prose form (e.g. as a `PRIVACY.md` file in this repository; see #868)\r\n- [x] include link to \"Privacy Policy\" in the frontend (see #868)\r\n- [ ] figure out if existing accounts need to add explicit consent to the new \"Privacy Policy\" and if so:\r\n  - [ ] add new field to the `users` table that tracks that consent\r\n  - [ ] add API to change consent status (can likely be added to something like `POST /account`)\r\n  - [ ] check consent status on next login (of token renewal) and prevent further actions before consent is given\r\n- [ ] send emails to all current users about the new \"Privacy Policy\"",
